# The micro-SDPA generator gives the V*S micro-gemm the packed row's alignment whenever the VALUE
# precision is four-bit: under u8 keys with i4 values it used the f16 row's (128 bytes) for a
# 132-byte row, and the verify pass read value rows that depended on the physical pages a request got

# Applied against the pinned runtime, build 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29, on top of
# patches/0003-0032. arcint 0.4.4 series (DESIGN.md section 7.0.2bu).
#
# What changes:
#   sdpa_gen_micro.cpp   One condition: problem_vs.A's alignment is the packed row (v_head_size *
#                       u4 + 4 bytes: 132 at head 256, 68 at 128) when the value cache is four-bit,
#                       not only when the key cache is. Patch 0020 keyed the operand's type
#                       (Ta_ext) on the value precision and left the alignment on the key's, so the
#                       served pairing (u8 keys by channel, i4 values by token) told the gemm
#                       strategy its rows were 128-byte aligned (alignment_for_ld returns the lowest
#                       set bit of head * 2, capped at 128). A strategy addressing 128-byte-aligned rows reads
#                       something that depends on the page's address: the agent configuration's
#                       greedy text alternated by request parity (the page pool is a stack, odd
#                       requests get ascending pages, even ones descending) and was wrong from the
#                       first request, MTP on differing from MTP off.
#   paged_attention_gpu_test.h
#                       The harness addressed cache pages as start + j in ten places and built
#                       only ascending contiguous block tables, so a kernel reading a neighbouring
#                       page passed every case; now every page goes through the table, num_blocks
#                       is the table's maximum, and permute_pages()/page_order give a test a
#                       reversed table or a gap after page 0 (the served pool's third request;
#                       ARCINT_TEST_PAGE_PERM overrides for exploration). The four-bit value
#                       packing of past tokens is adjacent pairs (byte n = dims 2n, 2n+1), as
#                       pa_kv_cache_update_ref.cl writes and the readers expect; it was
#                       (dim 32g + lane, dim 32g + 16 + lane), a layout no kernel reads, invisible
#                       while every dim of a token carried the same value.
#   paged_attention_gpu_test.cpp
#                       The mixed-micro tests' fill could not see a misread page: all past keys -1,
#                       past values 0, new keys by token % 16 only, a query of 8 (one-hot softmax on
#                       each page's last token). Now every token, head and page has its own key
#                       (within 4e-4 of the u8 by-channel grid) and value (all sixteen four-bit
#                       levels in every token-and-head row, stored exactly), a query of 1/64. Cases
#                       added: the served verify shapes at head 128 and the served geometry (24
#                       heads, 4 KV heads, head 256) under ascending, reversed and gapped tables.
#
# MEASURED 2026-09-08 on the 24 GB card:
#   Plugin test, full statistics over every element against the float reference: before the
#     line the u8:i4 cases err by 2.0-2.3 on 98-99 % of elements (value range 15) and the
#     served three-token case hangs the binary (aborts under a reversed or gapped table); with it
#     exact: at most 0.001 on every case, none over 1e-2. The same fill through f16 KV and through u8 KV: exact to the tolerance. The
#     tests' tolerance stays at 1e-2. (Retracted on the record, DESIGN 7.0.2bu: a first fill with
#     eight levels per row measured its own quantisation as a 0.11 "floor"; the review's
#     arithmetic reproduced the element map from the fill, sixteen levels per row removed it.)
#   Plugin test on the patch's exact content: u8:i4 mixed micro 14/14, u4 mixed micro 2/2,
#     paged_attention 255/255 under the default and under a reversed table, sdpa 47/47.
#   Served (arcint 0.4.3, IR agent model, u8:i4, MTP on, chunk 512, one process): 130 tokens,
#     six requests: 825b1747 x6 = the MTP-off text (before: two texts alternating, neither the
#     MTP-off one); 8,005 tokens twice: e8010a09, e8010a09 (before: d2845b6c); prefill 865/870
#     t/s against 869/874; decode at 8k 20-23 t/s against 21.6. Equivalence suite on the fixed
#     plugin: every gate, including the new "MTP at u8:i4: the same text on three requests of
#     one process"; on the unfixed plugin that gate fails and the rest pass.
#
# Package: +p15.

